### 5. Consolidate arg parsers between single and dual bringup

[_make_arg_parser()](file:///home/hz/cmu_exploration_ws/src/go2_issac_stack/scripts/isaac_t_world_dual_bringup.py#143-228) in single bringup (241 lines) and dual bringup (227 lines) share ~22 identical `add_argument` calls. The dual version adds `--robots-config`, `--robot-a-*`, `--robot-b-*`, and `--physics-device`.

#### Strategy: Shared base parser

```python
# in isaac_t_world_bringup.py (already imported by dual)
def _make_base_arg_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    """Common args shared by single and dual bringup."""
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)
    p.add_argument("--world-file", required=True, ...)
    p.add_argument("--robot-urdf", ...)
    ...  # ~20 shared args
    return p

def _make_arg_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(parents=[_make_base_arg_parser()], ...)
    p.add_argument("--ros-namespace", ...)
    p.add_argument("--spawn-x", ...)
    ...  # ~6 single-only args
    return p
```

#### [MODIFY] [isaac_t_world_dual_bringup.py](file:///home/hz/cmu_exploration_ws/src/go2_issac_stack/scripts/isaac_t_world_dual_bringup.py)

```python
def _make_arg_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(parents=[single._make_base_arg_parser()], ...)
    p.add_argument("--robots-config", ...)
    p.add_argument("--robot-a-namespace", ...)
    ...  # ~8 dual-only args
    return p
```

Net reduction: **~180 lines total** between the two files.

