### 6. Simplify [_robot_autonomy_actions](file:///home/hz/cmu_exploration_ws/src/go2_issac_stack/launch/two_go2_isaac_coordinated_autonomy.launch.py#35-338) in the dual launch file

[_robot_autonomy_actions](file:///home/hz/cmu_exploration_ws/src/go2_issac_stack/launch/two_go2_isaac_coordinated_autonomy.launch.py#35-338) in [two_go2_isaac_coordinated_autonomy.launch.py](file:///home/hz/cmu_exploration_ws/src/go2_issac_stack/launch/two_go2_isaac_coordinated_autonomy.launch.py) (lines 35–337, ~300 lines) builds the per-robot autonomy stack. It is mostly a long list of `if use_fast_lio ... else ...` blocks and node constructions, with many intermediate `LaunchConfiguration` objects repeated verbatim.

#### [MODIFY] [two_go2_isaac_coordinated_autonomy.launch.py](file:///home/hz/cmu_exploration_ws/src/go2_issac_stack/launch/two_go2_isaac_coordinated_autonomy.launch.py)

- Extract a `_slam_actions(ns, cfg, use_fast_lio, use_sim_time)` helper (~30 lines) for the SLAM branch logic.
- Use a list comprehension to build both robot autonomy blocks instead of repeating the same construction for `ROBOT_A_NS` and `ROBOT_B_NS`.
- No algorithm parameters change, only structural Python refactoring.

Net reduction: **~100 lines** in the dual launch file.

